tor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO TAMOTSU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HORIUCHI, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUTSUMI, MASAMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO, TAMOTSU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A secondary lithium battery comprising a positive electrode (1) capable of charging/discharging lithium ions, a negative electrode (2) comprising a material capable of being doped or undoped with lithium ions, lithium metal, etc., and an electrolyte through which lithium ions can move.  The negative electrode (2) contains an imide compound represented by chemical formula (1) wherein Z is -(CH2)n- (n is an integer of 2 to 7, 1,2-cyclohexylene, or 1,2-phenylene each of which may be substituted; and X is hydrogen or alkyl, aralkylcarbonyl, alkylcarbonyl, alkoxycarbonyl, aralkyloxycarbonyl, or imidyloxycarbonyl each of which may be substituted.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une batterie au lithium secondaire comprenant une électrode positive (1) capable de charger/décharger des ions lithium, une électrode négative (2) comprenant un matériau capable d'être dopé ou non dopé par des ions lithium, du lithium métal, etc., et un électrolyte au sein duquel peuvent migrer des ions lithium. L'électrode négative (2) renferme un composé imide de formule chimique (1), dans laquelle Z désigne -(CH2)n- (n désigne un nombre entier compris entre 2 et 7), le 1,2-cyclohexylène ou le 1,2-phénylène, chacun d'eux pouvant être substitué ; et X désigne l'hydrogène ou un alkyle, un aralkylcarbonyle, alkylcarbonyle, alcoxycarbonyle, aralkyloxycarbonyle ou un imidyloxycarbonyle, chacun d'eux pouvant être substitué.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>